<title>UK: Energy Group up on U.S. acquisition hopes.</title>
<headline>Energy Group up on U.S. acquisition hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in The Energy Group Plc rose on Monday after press reports that it was in the running to acquire U.S. power group New England Electric Systems, a move that would bolster its presence in the U.S., analysts said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 10-1/2p at 498-1/2 by 0956 GMT --- extending a rebound from its low point of 462p in the wake of its demerger from conglomerate Hanson Plc -- in moderate volume of 776,865 shares.</p>
<p>Analysts said there would be synergies between the U.S. group and both Energy Group's Peabody Coal unit in the U.S. and its Eastern Electricity unit in the UK.</p>
